commit 6845b62c5d5a9bf46c5ad0ef2bd4e6e8917a180c
Author: thesa <thesa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 6 21:16:17 2026 -0400

    feat(consistency): add shadow-only rain arbitrage detection for KXRAIN*M
    
    consistency._group_markets() blanket-excluded monthly rain-total ladders
    (KXRAIN*M), so rain arbitrage was never checked -- unlike temperature,
    whose ladders this same monotonicity check has protected for months.
    Live-verified first: every rain bracket across NYC/Chicago/St. Petersburg
    is strike_type="greater"; St. Petersburg's real July 2026 ladder had
    exactly 10 brackets, confirming the backlog entry's own "10 vs 4" framing.
    
    Ships as a shadow-only first pass (user's explicit design choice, since
    rain's ladder monotonicity has never been checked against live prices
    before): Violation gained an is_shadow field, set explicitly at grouping
    time for every entry (not re-derived downstream from key shape, so a
    future market family can't silently inherit is_shadow=False by omission).
    Rain groups via the existing sibling market_implied_rain_event_key()
    (city, "RAIN", year, month) key rather than a new one. All 3 real
    find_violations() consumers wired: main.py's arb-placement loop skips
    placement for shadow violations, trade_cycle.py's >5-violation circuit
    breaker excludes them from that count (so rollout noise can't halt real
    temperature auto-trading) while still logging both populations, and
    cmd_consistency's manual report marks shadow rows. Also fixed in passing:
    Violation.description hardcoded a "degrees" symbol that would have
    mislabeled rain's inches as Fahrenheit.
    
    Independent opus review (effort=high) found 1 HIGH + 6 MEDIUM + 8 LOW,
    all fixed:
    - HIGH: the rain branch's parse_market_price() call was unguarded --
      a single malformed rain price could raise out of find_violations()
      entirely, which via each caller's own broad exception handler could
      halt ALL auto-trading for the cycle or silently disable the whole arb
      block -- exactly what the shadow design existed to prevent. Fixed on
      both the new rain branch and the identical pre-existing unguarded call
      on the temperature branch (same fix, same file, in-scope adjacency).
    - MEDIUM: a zero-quote-leg phantom-edge bug (a one-sided book still
      reports has_quote=True, so a missing bid or ask could compute a
      fabricated "guaranteed" edge) -- fixed with an explicit two-sided-quote
      guard before emitting any violation. Two fail-closed guard tests were
      vacuous (used monotone prices that would've passed even with the guard
      deleted) -- rewritten with inversion-shaped prices. Added the one test
      proving main.py's arb loop actually skips placement for a shadow
      violation via the real cmd_watch path (previously zero coverage).
    - LOW: threshold formatting, silent-drop logging, log-sample balance
      between real/shadow violations, test fixture accuracy, a weak
      assertion, and 3 new circuit-breaker tests covering the mixed-population
      and exact-boundary cases.
    
    Filed a follow-up backlog entry for the graduation decision (when/how
    shadow rain violations start driving real auto-placement) rather than
    guessing at a mechanism upfront -- unlike this project's other
    shadow-then-graduate signals, a monotonicity violation has no obvious
    settlement outcome to correlate against, so the right shape needs real
    shadow observations to design against first.
    
    65 tests pass (8 new + 2 updated in test_consistency.py, 4 new in
    test_trade_cycle_engine.py); shadow-tagging and the shadow-skip fix were
    both mutation-tested by hand. ruff/ruff-format/mypy clean.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

